{
  "Next.js Pages Guide": {
    "prefix": "nextjspages",
    "description": "Guide for structuring Next.js pages with server and client components",
    "body": [
      "When creating or modifying Next.js pages, follow these steps and principles:",
      "",
      "1. Page Structure:",
      "   - Make the main page component a server component (no 'use client' directive)",
      "   - Handle authentication at the page level using getServerSession with authOptions",
      "   - Split interactive parts into client components",
      "   - Keep data fetching in the server component",
      "",
      "2. Data Fetching in Server Components:",
      "   - Use direct function calls instead of API routes",
      "   - Import and use database/service functions directly",
      "   - Handle errors and provide safe default values",
      "   - Avoid fetch calls in server components unless absolutely necessary",
      "",
      "3. Client Components:",
      "   - Create separate files for client components in a components folder",
      "   - Add 'use client' directive at the top",
      "   - Accept data as props from the server component",
      "   - Handle all interactive features (forms, state, effects)",
      "   - Use API routes for data mutations",
      "",
      "4. Props and Types:",
      "   - Define clear interfaces for component props",
      "   - Pass only necessary data to client components",
      "   - Handle null/undefined cases with default values",
      "   - Use proper session and user types from next-auth",
      "",
      "5. Error Handling:",
      "   - Implement error boundaries where needed",
      "   - Provide fallback UI for error states",
      "   - Log errors appropriately",
      "   - Return safe default values",
      "",
      "6. Authentication:",
      "   - Always import authOptions from @/lib/auth",
      "   - Use getServerSession(authOptions) for auth checks",
      "   - Redirect unauthenticated users",
      "   - Pass user data to components that need it",
      "",
      "7. File Organization:",
      "   - Place page component in app/[route]/page.tsx",
      "   - Create components/[route]/ for page-specific components",
      "   - Keep shared components in components/shared/",
      "   - Group related components together",
      "",
      "Example Structure:",
      "```typescript",
      "// app/settings/account/page.tsx",
      "import { getServerSession } from 'next-auth';",
      "import { authOptions } from '@/lib/auth';",
      "import { loadData } from '@/lib/data';",
      "",
      "export default async function Page() {",
      "  const session = await getServerSession(authOptions);",
      "  if (!session?.user) redirect('/auth/signin');",
      "",
      "  const data = await loadData(); // Direct function call",
      "",
      "  return (",
      "    <Layout>",
      "      <ServerComponent data={data} />",
      "      <ClientComponent",
      "        username={session.user.name}",
      "        initialData={data}",
      "      />",
      "    </Layout>",
      "  );",
      "}",
      "```",
      "",
      "```typescript",
      "// components/account/client-component.tsx",
      "'use client';",
      "",
      "interface Props {",
      "  username: string;",
      "  initialData: Data;",
      "}",
      "",
      "export function ClientComponent({ username, initialData }: Props) {",
      "  // Handle interactive features here",
      "}",
      "```",
      ""
    ]
  }
}
